# CLZERO—Zero Cache Line (AMD; not in the Intel SDM)
# AMD64 Architecture Programmer's Manual Vol. 3 (pub. 24594), "CLZERO":
# 'clears the cache line specified by the logical address in rAX' (the
# address size's rAX, in DS), aligned down to the line (64 bytes, CPUID
# 8000_0008h:EBX[0]); it faults as a store would. Eight 8-byte stores:
# v1's data cache is write-through (D-018), so they reach DRAM as stores do.
@opcodes
0F 01 FC | CLZERO | ZO | Valid | Valid
@encoding
ZO | N/A | N/A | N/A | N/A
@operation
a := RAX;
IF AddressSize = 16 THEN a := a AND FFFFH; FI;
IF AddressSize = 32 THEN a := a AND FFFFFFFFH; FI;
a := a AND FFFFFFFFFFFFFFC0H;
i := 0;
WHILE i < 64
DO
    p := a + i;                  (* 'DS:a + i' would parse as (DS:a) + i *)
    Memory64[DS:p] := 0;
    i := i + 8;
OD;
@flags
None.
